## 💻 Code Examples

### Train-Test Split & SVM Training
```python
from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split
from sklearn.svm import SVC
from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score

# Define target variable (y) and features (X)
y = ansur_df['Gender']
X = ansur_df.drop('Gender', axis=1)

# Split data into 70% training and 30% test sets
X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(X, y, test_size=0.3)

# Instantiate and fit the Support Vector Classifier
svc = SVC()
svc.fit(X_train, y_train)

# Evaluate model accuracy
train_accuracy = accuracy_score(y_train, svc.predict(X_train))
test_accuracy = accuracy_score(y_test, svc.predict(X_test))

print(f"Train Accuracy: {train_accuracy:.2f} | Test Accuracy: {test_accuracy:.2f}")
Dimensionality Reduction (Single Feature Selection)
Python
# Select a single informative feature to reduce dimensionality
X = ansur_df[['neckcircumferencebase']]

# Split, fit, and evaluate again
X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(X, y, test_size=0.3)
svc = SVC()
svc.fit(X_train, y_train)

accuracy_train = accuracy_score(y_train, svc.predict(X_train))
accuracy_test = accuracy_score(y_test, svc.predict(X_test))

print(accuracy_train, accuracy_test)
Automated Feature Selection with VarianceThreshold
